# MIT brand colors (Institute palette)

Authoritative reference: **[MIT Brand Guide — Color](https://brand.mit.edu/color)**.

## Core palette (web HEX)

Use these as the baseline for Institute-aligned reds, neutrals, and primary UI accents. Do **not** substitute legacy crimson hexes (e.g. `#a31f34`) unless reconciling historical assets—default UI tokens follow the guide.

| Name          | HEX       | Role on this site                                      |
| ------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| MIT Red       | `#750014` | `--primary` (light only), `--mit-red-core`, `Button variant="mit"`; brand marks — in **dark**, `--primary` is neutral; use `mit-*` / `variant="mit"` for institute red fills |
| Silver Gray   | `#8b959e` | Optional muted chrome / borders (expanded neutral)    |
| Bright Red    | `#ff1423` | Optional emphasis only — not default shell primary    |
| Black         | `#000000` | Pure black sparingly; prefer `--foreground` tokens   |
| White         | `#ffffff` | Surfaces and `*-foreground` on saturated reds        |

## Expanded palette

The guide’s **expanded palette** (blues, greens, purples, grays, etc.) is available for charts, illustrations, or secondary accents. Prefer semantic naming in CSS (`--chart-*`) or Tailwind theme slots rather than one-off hex in JSX.

## Implementation rules

1. **Single source of hex:** [`src/styles/mit-theme.css`](src/styles/mit-theme.css) (`:root` and `.dark`). Map utilities via `@theme inline` — no duplicate hex definitions in components.
2. **Components:** Prefer **`text-mit-red`**, **`bg-mit-red`** / **`Button variant="mit"`**, **`text-primary`**, **`border-border`** / **`border-mit-line`**, etc., over raw `#RRGGBB`. See [docs/mit-color-strategy.md](../../docs/mit-color-strategy.md) for light vs dark `primary`.
3. **TypeScript inline styles / SVG:** Use **`tokens.colors`** in [`src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts`](src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts) so values stay aligned with `mit-theme.css`.
4. **Accessibility:** Combine light and dark colors for legibility (see guide). Follow [ada-color-accessibility.mdc](ada-color-accessibility.mdc) — verify contrast on **default, hover, and focus** when reds are interactive.

